MEDICAL & NON-DIAGNOSTIC DEVICE DISCLAIMER
================================================================================

This Software is provided strictly for educational, experimental, and
informational self-screening purposes. It is NOT a regulated or cleared medical
device (such as under US FDA, EU MDR, or equivalent regulatory frameworks) and
is NOT intended to diagnose, treat, cure, mitigate, or prevent any disease,
refractive error, or ocular condition, nor to prescribe eyeglasses or contact
lenses.

Head-mounted displays (VR/AR headsets and optical see-through glasses) introduce
device-specific optical factors—including fixed focal planes (e.g., ~0.9 m to
4.0 m rather than clinical 6 m / 20 ft optical infinity), vergence-accommodation
differences, finite angular pixel density (PPD / Nyquist limits), lens sweet
spots, and ambient luminance variations—that differ from a calibrated clinical
examination lane.

Never disregard professional medical or optometric advice or delay seeking care
because of results shown by this Software. Always consult a licensed
optometrist, ophthalmologist, or qualified healthcare provider for comprehensive
vision testing and eye health evaluation.
